1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,600
You tap Send. But how does this photo actually reach your friend?

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:14,500
It travels as data, divided into small packets. Imagine numbered parcels carrying the information needed to rebuild your picture.

3
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:26,500
Through Wi-Fi or your mobile network, those packets enter the internet. Routers pass them between networks, toward your messaging app's servers.

4
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:36,500
If the route crosses an ocean, the data may travel through an underwater cable, carried by pulses of light.

5
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:45,500
Your friend's phone receives and reassembles the data. The app displays your photo.

6
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:50,800
A whole network behind one tiny action.

7
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:55,000
And it all starts when…
